          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life of Tenzin Gyatso</strong><br>\nTenzin Gyatso, born in 1935, is known as the 14th Dalai Lama. He was recognized as the reincarnation of the Dalai Lama at the age of two. His early life was spent in a monastic education, preparing for his role as Tibet's spiritual leader. Despite the religious focus, he also received a broad education, including science and Western subjects.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Becoming the Dalai Lama</strong><br>\nIn 1950, at the age of 15, Tenzin Gyatso was enthroned as the Dalai Lama. He assumed full political power over Tibet as the country faced threats of Chinese invasion. His leadership during this time was marked by efforts to modernize Tibet without losing its traditional culture.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Exile to India</strong><br>\nAfter the failed Tibetan uprising in 1959 against Chinese rule, the Dalai Lama fled to India. He established a government-in-exile in Dharamsala, which became a hub for Tibetan culture and resistance. This move also made the issue of Tibet known worldwide, drawing international support.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
