            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>The Dalai Lama and Science</strong><br>\nHe has a keen interest in science and has encouraged dialogue between science and Buddhism. This includes hosting conferences and discussions with scientists to explore how Buddhism and science can inform each other, particularly in understanding the mind and consciousness.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Cultural Impact and Preservation</strong><br>\nThe Dalai Lama has played a crucial role in the preservation of Tibetan culture. Through educational and cultural institutions, he has worked to maintain Tibetan language, art, and religious traditions for Tibetans in exile and in the homeland.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Later Years and Succession</strong><br>\nAs Tenzin Gyatso ages, the question of his succession becomes more pressing. He has suggested that the title of Dalai Lama might not continue after his death, which has led to discussions about the future leadership and representation of the Tibetan people.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
